model {
  extend basalt.modelGateway {
    metadata {
      constraint "Signed native membership reads prepare missing or pending mirrors for current selected non-provisioned secrets accounts before entering the organization transaction. The SDK owns mirror identity, expected-generation checks and retries; OAuth, retiring and mismatched bindings never acquire an inferred identity. The locked membership snapshot still rechecks current selections, generation, driver and binding identity and refuses incomplete authority. Reading again preserves account IDs, links, credentials and an already-ready mirror. Account-use inventories expose app selections only among the caller's already-visible apps and accounts, retaining restricted-grant narrowing. Encrypted operator binding inventories contain metadata and reference presence only; advisory-lock inventories select the requested organization's exact bigint access lock and expose no query text. The managed pool fixture serves its canonical provider catalog locally and releases mirrored accounts before their Home peer closes. Contract additions retain pure IIFE initializer wrappers so browser builds can eliminate unused schemas. The membership mirror preparation remains outside the organization transaction; only the subsequent locked reread can admit its current generation and binding for native use."
    }
  }
}
